`zh-cn`'s `LLLL` is `YYYY年M月D日ddddAh点mm分`, so the weekday is written immediately next to the day period: `2024年10月15日星期二下午2点25分`. Without `weekdaysParseExact`, the strict weekday token uses a generic word matcher and takes `星期二下午` as one word; the exact weekday lookup then fails, so every `LLLL` value this locale formats fails to parse back:

```js
moment([2024, 9, 15, 14, 25]).format('LLLL');
// '2024年10月15日星期二下午2点25分'
moment('2024年10月15日星期二下午2点25分', 'LLLL', 'zh-cn', true).isValid();
// false
```

`weekdaysParseExact: true` makes the weekday token match one of the listed names, leaving `下午` for the `A` token. This is the same cause as #6462 (ga/mt) and #6463 (tr), for the locale whose weekday is glued to the following token.

Tests: a new `parse LLLL with the weekday next to the day period` test covers all seven weekdays, checking both the parsed weekday and the retained date and time. On develop it fails 14 assertions; it passes with the flag. Full suite green (3945 tests, 165055 assertions); `eslint` and `prettier --check` clean.

